    "summary": "The Beatles' drummer and the model of song-first rock drumming. A natural left-hander on a right-handed kit, he leads fills with his left hand, which gives them their lopsided, tumbling character. Self-taught, ego-free, with steady time and a loose swing; his parts are written for each song and are as recognisable as the melodies."
